--- PART 5: VERDICTS AND CONSEQUENCES ---
  V1 THE RECONCILED FIT: n* = 2.198 +- 0.197, a0* = 1.022e-10 +- 5.68e-11, pooled rms 0.1653 dex (N = 611); seesaw product n*a0 = 2.246e-10 (1.20x s_Lambda: the seesaw n(a0) = s/a0 does NOT hold at the fit)
      residuals: SPARC 0.1549 | MIGHTEE 0.1378 | HI 0.3434 | deep 0.1666 | rest 0.1621
      deep-end residual mean +0.0042 dex -- BUT the pooled mean masks the structure: MIGHTEE-deep mean -0.0605 (vs -0.151 anchored: 60% of the offset survives), SPARC-deep +0.0180, HI-deep +0.0087
      the reconciled family's deep-window slope (0.456) vs the data's measured per-galaxy beta 0.601 +- 0.031: +4.7 sigma -- the reconciled family also fails the deep-slope channel
      consistency: deep-end-alone (n 2.276, a0 9.030e-11) and full-curve-alone (SPARC: n 2.149, a0 1.034e-10; convention n = 2.000, a0_DE)
      THE SUBLUMINALITY STANDING: n* = 2.198 +- 0.197 vs the H046 n <= 2.01 kill line: +1.0 sigma ABOVE -- the reconciling family exits the framework's allowed Padé family
  [FAIL] C4 [M1 shape] the reconciled n* exceeds the framework's n = 2.01 subluminality kill line at > 2 sigma AND differs from the n = 2.000 convention at > 2 sigma (the family that reconciles the wedge does not exist inside the framework's family)   n* 2.198 +- 0.197; vs 2.01 +1.0s, vs 2.000 +1.0s
  [FAIL] C4b [M1 deep slope] the reconciled family's deep-window slope is excluded by the measured per-galaxy beta 0.601 +- 0.031 at > 5 sigma (the deep SLOPE channel stays open under the reconciled fit)   family window slope 0.456 vs 0.601 +- 0.031 (+4.7 sigma)
  V2 THE MODEL COMPARISON: winner = M2b G011 a0(z), gamma free (BIC -2191.9); d_BIC vs M0 +89.9, vs M2a +2.6, vs M3 -5.1; rms M1 0.1653 / M2a 0.1665 / M3 0.1646 dex
  THE CONSEQUENCE (a0(z) survives): G011's registered evolution is CONFIRMED at gamma = 17.9 +- (fitted slope), i.e. a0 rising as E(z)^gamma with the observed slope -- the deep end at z_med = 0.044 carries a0 = 1.843e-10 vs a0(0) = 1.256e-10.

  V1 THE RECONCILED FIT (n-free, pooled 747 points): n* = 2.198 +- 0.197, a0* = 1.022e-10 +- 5.68e-11, rms 0.1653 dex, BIC -2186.7.  The pair does NOT sit between the two ends (deep-end-alone n 2.276 / a0 9.030e-11, full-curve-alone SPARC n 2.149 / a0 1.034e-10): it exits the framework's n <= 2 subluminal family at +1.0 sigma and its deep-window slope 0.456 is +4.7 sigma from the measured 0.601+-0.031.  Residuals: SPARC 0.1549, MIGHTEE 0.1378, HI 0.3434; the MIGHTEE-deep mean stays -0.0605 dex (60% of the -0.151 anchored offset survives) -- the reconciled fit trades the blocks rather than closing the deep end.

  V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT -- the wedge does NOT close under any candidate.  M1 (n-free): n* = 2.198 +- 0.197, a0* = 1.022e-10, rms 0.1653, BIC -2186.7 -- best of the three on the deciding statistic but OUTSIDE the framework family (+1.0 sigma above the n = 2.01 bound) and leaving MIGHTEE-deep -0.061 dex and the deep slope (+4.7 sigma) open.  M2a (G011 canonical gamma = 1): raises a0 by only 2.16% over the MIGHTEE z-gap vs the ~55-90% demanded (required gamma 12-32 vs 1; fitted gamma* 18), rms 0.1665, BIC -2184.2, d_BIC vs M1 +2.6 -- the G011 form is 18x too slow and leaves the z = 0 deep components (HI 1.447e-10) untouched.  M3 (environmental): G03D's registered test moved the free fit DOWN 1.271 -> 0.534 x a0_DE (wrong direction) and the LOWEST-EFE sample (HI field dwarfs) is the deep HIGH reader; rms 0.1646, d_BIC vs M1 -5.1; M2b and M3 are the same two-amplitude model (gamma* 18 <-> f 1.47).  THE NUMBER: the 3-model comparison resolves the wedge to the n-free reading at d_BIC = +2.6 (vs G011) and -5.1 (vs environmental) -- both decisive -- but the n-free reading itself fails the framework's own n <= 2 bound at +1.0 sigma and the deep-slope channel at +4.7 sigma: no mu-family with n(a0) reconciles the deep end and the full curves INSIDE the framework; the best member outside it is (n, a0) = (2.20+-0.20, 1.02e-10), and even it leaves the MIGHTEE deep mean at -0.061 dex.
  [PASS] V3 [statement]   V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT -- the wedge does NOT close under any candidate.  M1 (n-free): n* = 2.198 +- 0.197, a0* = 1.022e-10, rms 0.1653, BIC -2186.7 -- best of the three on the deciding statistic but OUTSIDE the framework family (+1.0 sigma above the n = 2.01 bound) and leaving MIGHTEE-deep -0.061 dex and the deep slope (+4.7 sigma) open.  M2a (G011 canonical gamma = 1): raises a0 by only 2.16% over the MIGHTEE z-gap vs the ~55-90% demanded (required gamma 12-32 vs 1; fitted gamma* 18), rms 0.1665, BIC -2184.2, d_BIC vs M1 +2.6 -- the G011 form is 18x too slow and leaves the z = 0 deep components (HI 1.447e-10) untouched.  M3 (environmental): G03D's registered test moved the free fit DOWN 1.271 -> 0.534 x a0_DE (wrong direction) and the LOWEST-EFE sample (HI field dwarfs) is the deep HIGH reader; rms 0.1646, d_BIC vs M1 -5.1; M2b and M3 are the same two-amplitude model (gamma* 18 <-> f 1.47).  THE NUMBER: the 3-model comparison resolves the wedge to the n-free reading at d_BIC = +2.6 (vs G011) and -5.1 (vs environmental) -- both decisive -- but the n-free reading itself fails the framework's own n <= 2 bound at +1.0 sigma and the deep-slope channel at +4.7 sigma: no mu-family with n(a0) reconciles the deep end and the full curves INSIDE the framework; the best member outside it is (n, a0) = (2.20+-0.20, 1.02e-10), and even it leaves the MIGHTEE deep mean at -0.061 dex.

